From de4872cf04a1b4814226863a7d9a55ee9e8a9390 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junyu Lai <junyulai@google.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 20:38:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Enforce permissions in IWifiP2pListener callback

IWifiP2pListener.onPersistentGroupsChanged is called when persistent
groups change. Currently, it broadcasts to all registered listeners
without enforcing signature permissions or redacting the own device's
MAC address.

Fix this by:
1. Storing the AttributionSource of the listener during registration.
2. Checking signature permissions before broadcasting.
3. Redacting the own device's MAC address if the listener lacks
   LOCAL_MAC_ADDRESS permission.

Bug: 515047710
Test: atest FrameworksWifiTests:com.android.server.wifi.p2p.WifiP2pServiceImplTest
Flag: EXEMPT CVE_FIX

TAG=agy
CONV=c08236f3-085e-436e-b7ee-60ef85e95c36

(also included test fix at ag/40738895)
(cherry picked from commit 964377f10006a5c944fa0b88803e5f6351e475b1)
Merged-In: I55bbffb01970876a4ba2aead2d86e95a40d22b8d
Change-Id: I55bbffb01970876a4ba2aead2d86e95a40d22b8d
